    "q-100856": {
      "dom_id": "step-q100856",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the formula for the $n$th term of the arithmetic sequence that has a $25$th term of $100$ and a common difference of $4.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since ${a}_{25}=100$ is $24$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{25} & ={a}_{1}+24d \\\\ 100 & ={a}_{1}+24(4) \\\\ 100 & ={a}_{1}+96 \\\\ 4 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =4+(n-1)(4) \\\\  & =4+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
